## Where this ran, and why not in the checkout

The repo's own Godot process (PID 94690, `res://game/Main.tscn -- --seed=20260916
--tier=3 --camera=default`) has been up since 2026-09-16 and was never touched. Every
engine run of this wave happened in an isolated copy of the working tree, so the
checkout cannot collect engine-generated files while that process holds the project:

    source  /Users/lucafantini/Desktop/Personal/Padel-3D/steam-circuit-padel-godot
            (rsync -a, excluding /.git and /godot/.godot; untracked UI sources included)
    copy    /tmp/padel-uir-wave2-20260917/repo
    check   tree manifest (relative path + sha256 per file): diff empty before the runs
    logs    /tmp/padel-uir-wave2-20260917/logs/

The commands below are the ticket's acceptance commands, run inside the copy; the verdict
is the audit's own `PASS n/n` line and exit code. The repo carries no `.godot/`,
`*.import` or `*.uid` artifact produced by this wave.

